\newlabel{tab:link}{{1}{5}{\textbf {Does better forecasting go with better simulation?} Rank correlation, within each world, between forecast error on the merchants' plans and each measure (higher is worse for every measure, so a positive number means better forecasters are also better at it), averaged over three seeds. Bold: the 95\% bootstrap interval excludes zero. --: every version made the same choice, so there is nothing to rank. All versions: the test fixed in the plan (12 world model, 12 LightGBM and the log-linear model). Within a model class: added after the first results}{table.caption.15}{}}
