\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The three models with the price rules, head to head, with the world as the unit} (added after the first results). Each cell: worlds in which the first model has the lower error on new plans, of all worlds (two-sided sign test), then the median paired difference in error (negative favours the first model) with a 95\% interval from a bootstrap over worlds. Base: one version of each model. Median and best: each model's median and best version on the held-out plans over 12 world model, 12 LightGBM and 6 log-linear versions. The kinked base comparison has 40 worlds (seeds 101 to 110); the tuned comparisons have 12.}}{8}{table.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:h2h}{{3}{8}{\textbf {The three models with the price rules, head to head, with the world as the unit} (added after the first results). Each cell: worlds in which the first model has the lower error on new plans, of all worlds (two-sided sign test), then the median paired difference in error (negative favours the first model) with a 95\% interval from a bootstrap over worlds. Base: one version of each model. Median and best: each model's median and best version on the held-out plans over 12 world model, 12 LightGBM and 6 log-linear versions. The kinked base comparison has 40 worlds (seeds 101 to 110); the tuned comparisons have 12}{table.caption.25}{}}
