\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Real data: error on the rarest plans that were actually run} (added after the first results; Appendix~\ref {app:plan}). Summed absolute error over summed sales, median over the forecast origins; lower is better. Deep cuts: every cut deeper than the threshold (30\% or 20\%) was removed from training and the held-out weeks with such a cut are scored; pure: with no circular or display, so price is the only lever that changed. Lasting moves: on the Frat, a recorded regular price 10\% or more from its last value, steady for four weeks before the origin and through every held-out week; on M5, a move of 5\% or more in a constructed regular price. These are sales that happened, not plans never run.}}{9}{table.caption.29}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:real}{{4}{9}{\textbf {Real data: error on the rarest plans that were actually run} (added after the first results; Appendix~\ref {app:plan}). Summed absolute error over summed sales, median over the forecast origins; lower is better. Deep cuts: every cut deeper than the threshold (30\% or 20\%) was removed from training and the held-out weeks with such a cut are scored; pure: with no circular or display, so price is the only lever that changed. Lasting moves: on the Frat, a recorded regular price 10\% or more from its last value, steady for four weeks before the origin and through every held-out week; on M5, a move of 5\% or more in a constructed regular price. These are sales that happened, not plans never run}{table.caption.29}{}}
